## 9. When to Use Random Forest Regression

### ✅ Use it when:
- You have **tabular/structured data**
- You need a **strong baseline** quickly
- Your data has **non-linear relationships**
- You want **feature importance** out of the box
- You don't want to worry about feature scaling

### ❌ Avoid it when:
- You need to **extrapolate** beyond training data range (use gradient boosting or neural nets)
- **Interpretability is critical** (use linear regression or a single decision tree)
- Data is **very high-dimensional sparse** text/image data (use deep learning)
- **Real-time inference** is required with very strict latency (it's slower than linear models)

